Copyright 2026 local-multimodal-infra contributors

This package collects data and model files from the projects below. Each file
keeps the license of its sources; see README.md for the per-file table and
LICENSES/ for the full texts. The files were produced by
scripts/local/zh_frontend_export.py in
https://github.com/mercallureAI/local-multimodal-infra; the changes made to
each source are stated here as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) and CC BY-SA 4.0
section 3(a)(1)(B) require.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WeTextProcessing / wetext                                  Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
wetext/{zh,en}/tn/{tagger,verbalizer}.fst
  Text normalization FSTs built by WeTextProcessing
  (https://github.com/wenet-e2e/WeTextProcessing) and distributed with the
  Python package wetext 0.1.0 (https://github.com/pengzhendong/wetext).
  Copied unchanged.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
g2pW                                                       Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
g2pw/g2pw_int8.onnx
  g2pW polyphone model (https://github.com/GitYCC/g2pW; G2PWModel version
  v3.0), dynamically quantized to INT8. The INT8
  graph is the one published on ModelScope as pengzhendong/g2pw
  (G2PWModel/g2pw_int8.onnx, SHA-256 000a3dc34bebf3adf8a898d17b6be77c527b
  7d15ddd672b6abf028a73b81a8e1). Copied unchanged.
g2pw/meta.json
  Generated from g2pW's POLYPHONIC_CHARS.txt and MONOPHONIC_CHARS.txt and the
  bopomofo-to-pinyin map of the g2pw Python package: labels, per-character
  label masks and monophonic readings, with bopomofo converted to pinyin.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BERT (bert-base-chinese)                                   Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
g2pw/vocab.txt
  WordPiece vocabulary of bert-base-chinese
  (https://github.com/google-research/bert), the g2pW encoder's tokenizer.
  Copied unchanged.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PaddleSpeech                                               Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
paddlespeech/polyphonic.tsv, pinyin/t2s.tsv
  From PaddleSpeech (https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleSpeech) at commit
  6b25a400008d393f9c3af837b3c692b17f29ee1a:
  paddlespeech/t2s/frontend/polyphonic.yaml converted to TSV, and the
  traditional-to-simplified character pairs of
  paddlespeech/t2s/frontend/zh_normalization/char_convert.py written as TSV.
  The custom phrase readings PaddleSpeech's zh_frontend.py loads into
  pypinyin are included in pinyin/phrases.tsv.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
g2p-mix                                                    Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mainland/phrases.tsv
  g2p_mix/dict/phrases.txt of g2p-mix (https://github.com/pengzhendong/g2p-mix)
  at commit 0893439a6d1336670ac755b60156f08beec2ac87, readings rewritten in
  numbered-tone pinyin (TONE3, neutral tone as 5).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pypinyin, pinyin-data, phrase-pinyin-data, pypinyin-dict   MIT
Unicode Han Database (Unihan)                              Unicode-3.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pinyin/chars.tsv
  Single-character readings of pypinyin 0.55.0
  (https://github.com/mozillazg/python-pinyin), whose character data comes
  from pinyin-data (https://github.com/mozillazg/pinyin-data), largely
  derived from the Unicode Han Database. Each character's default reading
  under PaddleSpeech's pypinyin configuration, written as TONE3.
mainland/readings.tsv
  Readings from the kTGHZ2013 field, else kXHC1983, of the Unicode Han
  Database, as packaged by pypinyin-dict 0.9.0
  (https://github.com/mozillazg/pypinyin-dict), written as TONE3.

  Unicode Han Database: Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc.
  https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CC-CEDICT                                                  CC BY-SA 4.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pinyin/phrases.tsv
  Phrase readings of pypinyin 0.55.0 with the large_pinyin dictionary of
  pypinyin-dict 0.9.0 loaded, as PaddleSpeech configures it. large_pinyin
  comes from phrase-pinyin-data (https://github.com/mozillazg/phrase-pinyin-data),
  which merges, among other sources, readings collected from zdic.net and
  CC-CEDICT. Each phrase's reading was resolved by pypinyin and written as
  TONE3; phrases whose reading does not cover every character were dropped.

  CC-CEDICT, published by MDBG (https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict).
  Referenced work: CEDICT, Copyright (C) 1997, 1998 Paul Andrew Denisowski.
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
